> Dear Elias,
>
> if I understand properly, when I have a graph with more than one
> connected compoment INLA automatically introduce a sum-to-zero
> constraint for each subgraph "j". However, INLA is considering the
> same variance (or precision) parameter for the data in each subgraph
> i.e. S_ij ~ ICAR(sd). For this reason, I would like to introduce more
> flexibility into the model by estimating a diferent variance (or
> precision) parameter for each disconnected component "j" i.e.  S_ij ~
> ICAR(sd_j).

Hi,

this is controlled by the option in f(..., adjust.for.con.comp=TRUE), if
set to FALSE, then there is just one sum-to-zero constr and the
correction for disconnected subgraphs is disabled.

if you have several subgraphs with different variances, and these are
disconnected, then you have to use several f()'s, like
f(i, model="besag") + f(j, ....) + f(....)

H

